IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P2-art-21.l4 -- ARTICLE 21 OF REGULATION (EU) 2016/679: RIGHT TO OBJECT (layer 1).
-- Written by P2 (Sonnet 5.5).  Lines 263-270 of eu-gdpr-2016-679-consolidated-20160504.txt (the Section 4 heading at
-- 261-262 and the two heading lines of Article 21 at 263-264 are `inert` headings).
-- Target compiler: main (build 1.6.112).  Answers: MAYBE BOOLEAN; a DEONTIC for the two SHANT rules.
-- WHOSE.  The data subject's CLAIM to object, and the controller's duty to stop processing once the data subject has
-- objected (the correlative; paragraphs 1 (second sentence) and 3).  Article 11(2) does not reach Article 21 ("Articles 15
-- to 20"), so no function here takes it.
-- PARAGRAPH 3 and 4 are passive in part: paragraph 3 names no party ("the personal data shall no longer be processed"); the
-- controller is assumed as the party of the SHANT, as in P1's Art 9(1) (fork F21-2); paragraph 4 is a decision function only.
-- READING A RESULT (NOTES).  NOTHING means the Regulation does not answer on these facts; never read it as no.
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Art 21 action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 21(1) process the personal data after the objection`
    `Art 21(3) process the personal data for direct marketing purposes after the objection`

§ `Article 21(1): objection to processing based on point (e) or (f) of Article 6(1)`

-- src:265 | The data subject shall have the right to object, on grounds relating to his or her particular situation, at any time to processing of personal data concerning him or her which is based on point (e) or (f) of Article 6(1), including profiling based on those provisions.
@ref Art 21(1) first sentence (src:265)
GIVEN `the person is the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the objection is on grounds relating to the data subject's particular situation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 6(1)(e) point (e) applies: the processing is necessary for a task in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 21(1) the data subject has the right to object, on grounds relating to his or her particular situation, to processing which is based on point (e) or (f) of Article 6(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is the data subject` AND `the body is the controller`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The data subject shall have the right to object": a grant to the data subject, against the controller who processes (entitlement-named, fork F15-1)
        IF NOT (`the objection is on grounds relating to the data subject's particular situation`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on grounds relating to his or her particular situation": an objection on other grounds is outside the grant, and the text does not say no to it
        IF `Art 6(1)(e) point (e) applies: the processing is necessary for a task in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to processing of personal data concerning him or her which is based on point (e) or (f) of Article 6(1)": processing on another basis is outside the sentence (paragraph 2 gives a separate right for direct marketing), and the text does not say no to it
    -- "at any time": the right may be exercised whenever; no date is read.  "including profiling based on those provisions": the right covers profiling too; not read (a list that includes).

-- src:265 | The controller shall no longer process the personal data unless the controller demonstrates compelling legitimate grounds for the processing which override the interests, rights and freedoms of the data subject or for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims.
@ref Art 21(1) second sentence (src:265)
GIVEN `the data subject has objected to the processing pursuant to Article 21(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller demonstrates compelling legitimate grounds for the processing which override the interests, rights and freedoms of the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller demonstrates compelling legitimate grounds for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 21(1) the controller shall no longer process the personal data unless the controller demonstrates compelling legitimate grounds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the data subject has objected to the processing pursuant to Article 21(1)`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence follows the data subject's objection; before any objection the text does not say the controller must stop
        IF `the controller demonstrates compelling legitimate grounds for the processing which override the interests, rights and freedoms of the data subject` OR `the controller demonstrates compelling legitimate grounds for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "unless"): "unless the controller demonstrates compelling legitimate grounds for the processing which override the interests, rights and freedoms of the data subject or for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a flat negative; JUST TRUE here means the controller is barred): "The controller shall no longer process the personal data"

GIVEN `Art 21(1) the controller shall no longer process the personal data unless the controller demonstrates compelling legitimate grounds` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 21 action`
`Art 21(1) the controller must no longer process the personal data after the objection` MEANS
    IF `Art 21(1) the controller shall no longer process the personal data unless the controller demonstrates compelling legitimate grounds` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY controller
         SHANT `Art 21(1) process the personal data after the objection`
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- a SHANT with no deadline is breached by the act itself

§ `Article 21(2) and (3): direct marketing`

-- src:266 | 2. Where personal data are processed for direct marketing purposes, the data subject shall have the right to object at any time to processing of personal data concerning him or her for such marketing, which includes profiling to the extent that it is related to such direct marketing.
@ref Art 21(2) (src:266)
GIVEN `the person is the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data are processed for direct marketing purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 21(2) the data subject has the right to object at any time to processing of personal data concerning him or her for direct marketing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is the data subject` AND `the body is the controller`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the data subject shall have the right to object": a grant to the data subject (entitlement-named, fork F15-1)
        IF NOT (`the personal data are processed for direct marketing purposes`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b); an entitlement-named function, fork F15-1): "Where personal data are processed for direct marketing purposes, the data subject shall have the right to object at any time"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    -- "which includes profiling to the extent that it is related to such direct marketing": a list that includes; not read.

-- src:267 | 3. Where the data subject objects to processing for direct marketing purposes, the personal data shall no longer be processed for such purposes.
@ref Art 21(3) (src:267)
GIVEN `the data subject objects to processing for direct marketing purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 21(3) the personal data shall no longer be processed for direct marketing purposes` MEANS
    IF `the data subject objects to processing for direct marketing purposes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a flat negative; JUST TRUE here means they are barred): "the personal data shall no longer be processed for such purposes"
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b)): "Where the data subject objects to processing for direct marketing purposes, the personal data shall no longer be processed for such purposes"

GIVEN `the data subject objects to processing for direct marketing purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 21 action`
`Art 21(3) the controller must no longer process the personal data for direct marketing purposes after the objection` MEANS
    IF `Art 21(3) the personal data shall no longer be processed for direct marketing purposes` `the data subject objects to processing for direct marketing purposes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY controller
         SHANT `Art 21(3) process the personal data for direct marketing purposes after the objection`
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- the party is assumed (fork F21-2): paragraph 3 is passive; a SHANT with no deadline is breached by the act itself

§ `Article 21(4) to (6)`

-- src:268 | 4. At the latest at the time of the first communication with the data subject, the right referred to in paragraphs 1 and 2 shall be explicitly brought to the attention of the data subject and shall be presented clearly and separately from any other information.
@ref Art 21(4) (src:268)
GIVEN `the right referred to in paragraphs 1 and 2 is explicitly brought to the attention of the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right is presented clearly and separately from any other information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this is done at the latest at the time of the first communication with the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 21(4) the right to object is explicitly brought to the attention of the data subject, clearly and separately, at the latest at the time of the first communication` MEANS
    IF `the right referred to in paragraphs 1 and 2 is explicitly brought to the attention of the data subject`
       AND `the right is presented clearly and separately from any other information`
       AND `this is done at the latest at the time of the first communication with the data subject`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "At the latest at the time of the first communication with the data subject, the right referred to in paragraphs 1 and 2 shall be explicitly brought to the attention of the data subject and shall be presented clearly and separately from any other information"
    -- passive: no party is named, so there is no regulative rule (fork F21-1)

-- src:269 | 5. In the context of the use of information society services, and notwithstanding Directive 2002/58/EC, the data subject may exercise his or her right to object by automated means using technical specifications.
@ref Art 21(5) (src:269)
GIVEN `the context is the use of information society services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 21(5) the data subject may exercise the right to object by automated means using technical specifications` MEANS
    IF `the context is the use of information society services`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the context of the use of information society services": another context is outside the grant, and the text does not say no to it
    -- "notwithstanding Directive 2002/58/EC": Directive 2002/58/EC is not among the sources; it is not read.

-- src:270 | 6. Where personal data are processed for scientific or historical research purposes or statistical purposes pursuant to Article 89(1), the data subject, on grounds relating to his or her particular situation, shall have the right to object to processing of personal data concerning him or her, unless the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out for reasons of public interest.
@ref Art 21(6) (src:270)
GIVEN `the person is the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose of the processing` IS AN `Art 5(1)(b) purpose of archiving, research or statistics`
      `the processing is pursuant to Article 89(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the objection is on grounds relating to the data subject's particular situation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out for reasons of public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 21(6) the data subject has the right to object to processing for scientific or historical research purposes or statistical purposes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is the data subject` AND `the body is the controller`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the data subject ... shall have the right to object": a grant to the data subject (entitlement-named, fork F15-1)
        IF NOT (    (    `the purpose of the processing` EQUALS `Art 5(1)(b) scientific research purposes`
                      OR `the purpose of the processing` EQUALS `Art 5(1)(b) historical research purposes`
                      OR `the purpose of the processing` EQUALS `Art 5(1)(b) statistical purposes`)
                AND `the processing is pursuant to Article 89(1)`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b); an entitlement-named function, fork F15-1): "Where personal data are processed for scientific or historical research purposes or statistical purposes pursuant to Article 89(1)": archiving purposes in the public interest are not on the list
        IF NOT (`the objection is on grounds relating to the data subject's particular situation`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on grounds relating to his or her particular situation": an objection on other grounds is outside the grant
        IF `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out for reasons of public interest`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "unless"): "unless the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out for reasons of public interest"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
